{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact G3b retained-selector head 9a125800a5d16792bcc6733f9344f6b2b49e4bc2 on builder/g3b-retained-selector-20261103, tree 3704f8d5, for source child 40051d7f under promise 078c5b2f and review request f6d25faf. This approval covers the local selector repair, its witnesses and the limited gate follow-up. It claims no creation retry, no live same-home continuation, no App key use, no deployment and no G3, Goose or archive acceptance. The planner still owns ruling request 1be877e9.\n\nScope. Main 916343cf is an ancestor, the worktree is clean, and the branch is pushed. Against main, the head changes claim.ts, its selector test, the archive scale test, one security seal, the generated Page bundle, the note and three manifests. The commit-message check passes for all three commits. No card path changes. Page browser run 41726457947 succeeds at 4e795071, and no Page or claim runtime input changes after that commit.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The first G3b create actually exits 1 after one Register GET returns 403, with no write. The retained plan is platform:register@25 with keys policy, and the old selector accepted neither that pin nor that policy.\n- The keys exception mirrors the Register's own founding-policy rule: keys passes only when the signing actor is among founders. The selector also requires @25, host none and an empty namespace, so it is narrower than the Register. Every earlier signature, service, seed, attempt, acknowledgement and receipt check still runs.\n- The selector returns register revision 1, so I checked that @25 keeps that revision. I diffed the platform definitions of @24 and @25. They differ only in the claim genesis reference, the host-choice and found-repository-choice guards, the namespace effect and the directory send. None of those touch the register item, so @25 holds revision 1 exactly as @24 does.\n- A wrong selection grants nothing. The Native Register still judges the fresh found and refuses an operator who is not a founder.\n- The four selector cases pass. Two direct controls distinguish: removing the @25 pin fails both repository-binding cases, and replacing the founder check with a non-empty test fails the keys case. Both controls run the same four tests and restore claim.ts to sha256 ac1a73d0…. The first wrapper control stays on record as inconclusive.\n- The archive change is test-only observation under ruling 15cee681. It records the first lower failure and any backward clock pair, and keeps every allowance and assertion. Parent 64552d40 stays open.\n\nThe gate exception. The gate at 4e795071, tree 0f2073fc, reads exit 1. Node ran all 133 cases, and its one failure is the security inventory's claim.ts seal. The owner's own failure message prints actual 13400cce…846dbe, and the head adopts exactly that value. From 4e795071 to the follow-up head 58e079d2, tree 0d058f83, only that seal line and the note change. scripts/test.mjs lists the test file, and no file imports it. The file needs no compiler context. The follow-up ran the whole security owner (11 pass) and the three unreached stages: Counting 56, plain 3,607 with one skip, Native 1,070 with two skips. Its actualExit reads 0, with the source unchanged before and after. The record keeps the failed gate as a failure. This repair meets every condition in docs/testing.md \"Follow-up after a gate\". The change keeps the case and its assertion, and updates the seal to the reviewed source, which is the change the assertion asks for.\n\nEvidence. The three manifests list 74 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. The 92 private originals (81 gate and follow-up files, 11 first-create files) match their indexes and are read-only. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match. The note names all three manifests' SHA-256 values: 446a9928…, 562a08d2… and 7a165c67…. The two custody limits stay stated as limits: the replaced local start record, and the 23 stage originals first written to OS temp, which now have verified durable copies.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Selection stays a local choice of revision from verified custody, and authority stays with the Register.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The exception admits fewer installs than the Register's own policy would, and a wrong local choice only earns a refusal.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The keys exception requires host none and an empty namespace, but the open path on @25 does not. That asymmetry matches the one G3b plan and is safe, because both paths hand the final judgment to the Register.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9f7c195dbdda2e7321685ed3438dd4cdee8ce2c5","binding":"assigned","head":"9a125800a5d16792bcc6733f9344f6b2b49e4bc2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7968b120e0e4841703e9773b707ff1ff19cbe118\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:078c5b2f8308c85f3076ea45ab5b9a235dd4b34f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7968b120e0e4841703e9773b707ff1ff19cbe118","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}